    "result": "I implemented `parse_line` in `solution.py` and wrote 61 pytest tests in `tests/test_solution.py`; `python -m pytest -q tests` passes with all 61. The implementation uses two small helpers, `_read_quoted` for quoted fields (handling `\"\"` escapes and the closing-quote check) and `_read_plain` for unquoted fields (rejecting `\"`, `\\r` and `\\n`), and `parse_line` does the type and separator validation before splitting. The tests cover the spec's examples, empty and trailing fields, whitespace preservation, custom separators, every listed `ValueError` case and both `TypeError` cases. I could not run the coverage, CRAP, mutation or bandit gates because the shell is restricted to the test command, so those are unverified. By reading the code, every line of `solution.py` is exercised by the tests and the functions are low in complexity, so I expect them to pass, but that is an inference, not a measurement.",
